## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a DP with variable-length segments and per-segment value, plus both memoized and tabulated solutions.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic programming over positions with limited jump length
- Maintaining per-iteration maximums within a window
- Bottom-up and top-down (memoization) DP variants

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumPartition(arr, k) {
  const n = arr.length;
  const dp = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    let maxInWin = -Infinity;
    for (let t = 1; t <= k && i + t <= n; t++) {
      maxInWin = Math.max(maxInWin, arr[i + t - 1]);
      dp[i] = Math.max(dp[i], maxInWin + dp[i + t]);
    }
  }
  return dp[0];
}
```

